---
# Templated by the `k3s` role (#178, ADR-0011). k3s's own bundled Traefik
# AddOn is customized through its documented HelmChartConfig mechanism, not
# Flux: Traefik stays outside GitOps (docs/reference/platform-state.md's
# "Known gap: three components outside GitOps"), same as ADR-0011's own
# Consequences section left this configuration for "the installing ticket".
# metadata.name/namespace must match the traefik HelmChart k3s itself
# creates (kube-system/traefik) for this to be picked up as an override
# rather than a separate, inert chart.
#
# k3s auto-applies any manifest dropped in its server manifests directory;
# this file must never be named traefik.yaml, the AddOn's own manifest that
# k3s overwrites with defaults on every start.
#
# Always templated, unlike the ACME block below (#264): the memory cap is
# the fix for a real BestEffort/OOM-killer exposure and has no dependency
# on a domain existing, so it can't wait behind #162's still-unbought one
# (docs/reference/platform-state.md's svclb exception note has the other
# half of that ticket). Only the ACME-specific keys stay conditional.
apiVersion: helm.cattle.io/v1
kind: HelmChartConfig
metadata:
  name: traefik
  namespace: kube-system
spec:
  valuesContent: |-
    # 61 MiB observed (#264). Request stays at 64Mi, the number the
    # platform-pods budget below is built on; the limit goes to 128Mi
    # instead of matching it, because 64Mi over 61Mi observed is ~5%
    # headroom and (once ACME below is configured) Traefik re-requests its
    # wildcard cert from scratch on every restart, a spike this budget
    # can't afford to OOM on. ADR-0020's platform-pods table reserves
    # memory "as pod requests" (its own table header), not limits, so
    # widening the limit alone doesn't touch that reservation. No CPU
    # request/limit either way: ADR-0002 deliberately runs no CPU quota, so
    # this pod (like every other memory-only-capped pod in the repo) is
    # QoS class Burstable, not Guaranteed.
    #
    # Platform-pods line, ADR-0020's 1 GiB envelope, by request: coredns
    # 70Mi + metrics-server 70Mi + cloudflared 64Mi + the smoke target 16Mi
    # + backup CronJobs 736Mi + this 64Mi = 1020Mi, a 4Mi margin.
    resources:
      requests:
        memory: 64Mi
      limits:
        memory: 128Mi
{% if k3s_traefik_acme_configured | bool %}
    # The wildcard domain lives under ports.websecure.http.tls, not under
    # certificatesResolvers.cloudflare.acme: `domains` isn't a field of the
    # resolver's own static acme config (verified against
    # traefik-helm-chart's values.yaml and Traefik's own acme reference
    # docs, which only document `domains` per-router or per-entrypoint):
    # setting it at the entrypoint makes it Traefik's default for every
    # router on websecure that doesn't name its own domains, which is what
    # pre-provisions the wildcard cert at startup instead of waiting for
    # the first IngressRoute to ask for one.
    #
    # ponytail: no persistence for /data/acme.json. #19 (storage layout)
    # hasn't settled a StorageClass yet, and this role already disables the
    # local-storage AddOn (defaults/main.yml). Traefik re-requests the
    # wildcard cert from scratch on every pod restart until then, which
    # risks Let's Encrypt's 5-duplicate-certificate/week rate limit if
    # restarts get frequent. Add `persistence.enabled: true` + a
    # storageClass once #19 gives one to point at.
    env:
      - name: {{ k3s_traefik_cloudflare_secret_key }}
        valueFrom:
          secretKeyRef:
            name: {{ k3s_traefik_cloudflare_secret_name }}
            key: {{ k3s_traefik_cloudflare_secret_key }}
    certificatesResolvers:
      cloudflare:
        acme:
          email: "{{ k3s_traefik_acme_email }}"
          dnsChallenge:
            provider: cloudflare
          storage: /data/acme.json
    ports:
      websecure:
        http:
          tls:
            certResolver: cloudflare
            domains:
              - main: "{{ k3s_traefik_domain }}"
                sans:
                  - "*.{{ k3s_traefik_domain }}"
{% endif %}
